# Response headers Cloudflare Workers static assets add when serving apps/web/dist (wrangler.jsonc `assets`).
#
# The page's Content-Security-Policy is the meta tag vite.config.ts injects into index.html (the one source of the
# policy); a header here carries only frame-ancestors, which a meta tag cannot express, plus the headers that are
# not CSP. Every path gets them: the single-page-application fallback serves index.html for app routes, and the
# headers are harmless on scripts, styles and images. Hashed bundles under /assets/ are immutable by construction.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: same-origin

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
